  "confidences": {"U": 0.9, "A": 0.95, "C": 0.8, "V": 0.95},
  "rationales": {"U":"'These UAVs shall include...' lacks antecedent reference — 'These' implies prior enumeration not provided in this requirement; reader cannot determine scope without external context. Evidence: 'These UAVs'.","A":"Ambiguity arises from parenthetical renaming ('henceforth referred to as Outrider and Predator respectively') which conflates TUAV with Outrider and MAE UAV with Predator without explicit confirmation of one-to-one mapping; 'associated payloads' and 'other network communication systems' are undefined and open-ended. Evidence: 'Tactical Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (TUAV) and the Medium Altitude and Endurance (MAE) UAV (henceforth referred to as Outrider and Predator respectively), their associated payloads, and other network communication systems'.","C":"The requirement does not contradict known facts (e.g., Predator is historically a MAE UAV), but 'Outrider' is not a standard public designation for TUAV — may reflect program-specific nomenclature; absence of authoritative source or definition introduces mild correctness risk. Evidence: 'henceforth referred to as Outrider and Predator respectively'.","V":"No testable criterion is specified: no measurable attributes (e.g., count, interface protocols, data rates, physical interfaces), no pass/fail condition, and 'other network communication systems' is inherently unverifiable due to open scope. Evidence: 'and other network communication systems'."}, 
  "suggestions": {"U":"Replace 'These UAVs' with explicit subject: 'The system shall comprise the following UAV types:' followed by enumerated, self-contained items.","A":"Replace entire clause with atomic, named, bounded elements: 'The system shall include exactly two UAV platforms: (a) the Tactical Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (TUAV), designated Outrider; and (b) the Medium Altitude and Endurance (MAE) UAV, designated Predator. Each UAV shall be integrated with its vendor-specified primary electro-optical/infrared (EO/IR) payload and embedded UHF/VHF data link. No additional UAV platforms are permitted.'","C":"Retain current names only if traceably aligned to a referenced configuration baseline document (e.g., 'per Configuration Baseline v2.1, Section 3.2'); otherwise replace 'Outrider' with the formally approved program name or omit alias. Suggestion: 'the Tactical Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (TUAV), as defined in System Specification SS-2023-04, Section 4.1'.","V":"Replace with verifiable statements: 'The system shall include one TUAV unit (model: RQ-7B Shadow) and one MAE UAV unit (model: MQ-1B Predator), each delivering real-time video via a Line-of-Sight IP-based data link operating at ≥1.2 Mbps sustained throughput, verified via packet capture and throughput measurement during Integration Test ST-07.'"},
  "issues": [
    {"type":"U","evidence":"These UAVs","rewrite":"The system shall comprise the following UAV types:"},
    {"type":"A","evidence":"TUAV and the Medium Altitude and Endurance (MAE) UAV (henceforth referred to as Outrider and Predator respectively), their associated payloads, and other network communication systems","rewrite":"The system shall include exactly two UAV platforms: (a) the Tactical Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (TUAV), designated Outrider; and (b) the Medium Altitude and Endurance (MAE) UAV, designated Predator. Each UAV shall be integrated with its vendor-specified primary electro-optical/infrared (EO/IR) payload and embedded UHF/VHF data link. No additional UAV platforms are permitted."},
    {"type":"V","evidence":"other network communication systems","rewrite":"The system shall include one TUAV unit (model: RQ-7B Shadow) and one MAE UAV unit (model: MQ-1B Predator), each delivering real-time video via a Line-of-Sight IP-based data link operating at ≥1.2 Mbps sustained throughput, verified via packet capture and throughput measurement during Integration Test ST-07."}
  ]
}
